#: ../../adr/0002-state-and-pure-transfers.md:1
msgid "ADR-0002: Element state and pure transfer functions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0002-state-and-pure-transfers.md:3
msgid "**Status**: accepted"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0002-state-and-pure-transfers.md:4
msgid "**Date**: 2026-10-16"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0002-state-and-pure-transfers.md:5
msgid "**Plan step**: P1.4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0002-state-and-pure-transfers.md:7
msgid "Context"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0002-state-and-pure-transfers.md:9
msgid ""
"Elements carry configuration (focal length, velocity...) and a mutable "
"state changed by actions (stage position, shutter open...). They must "
"also compute how they act on light. Requirements REQ-EL-8 and REQ-EL-10 "
"ask for pure numerical transfer functions, so that they can be JIT-"
"compiled, vectorised (`vmap`), differentiated (JAX) and run in parallel; "
"REQ-EL-5 and REQ-EL-7 ask for actions that change the state, in "
"simulation as well as in operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0002-state-and-pure-transfers.md:15
msgid "Decision"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0002-state-and-pure-transfers.md:17
msgid ""
"**Fields** are declared on the class: `Param` (configuration), `State` "
"(changed by actions) and `Setting` (non-physical). Each assignment "
"validates the value, stores the user value and its SI form, and calls "
"`_on_field_changed` (cache invalidation)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0002-state-and-pure-transfers.md:20
msgid ""
"**Transfer functions are `staticmethod`s** with the signature "
"`transfer(values, inputs) -> outputs`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0002-state-and-pure-transfers.md:21
msgid ""
"`values` is an immutable `Values` snapshot of the SI values of every "
"field (params, state, settings);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0002-state-and-pure-transfers.md:22
msgid "`inputs` and `outputs` map port names to signals."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0002-state-and-pure-transfers.md:24
msgid ""
"Being static, a transfer function cannot read or modify the element: "
"everything it depends on is in its arguments. Declaring a non-static "
"`transfer` raises `TypeError` when the class is created."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0002-state-and-pure-transfers.md:26
msgid ""
"**State changes only through assignments** (and later actions), never "
"inside a transfer function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0002-state-and-pure-transfers.md:27
msgid ""
"`Element.apply(**inputs)` runs the transfer on the current values and "
"checks port names and signal types. The execution engine (phase 5) calls "
"`transfer` directly with snapshots it caches."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0002-state-and-pure-transfers.md:29
msgid ""
"Elements refuse unknown public attributes (typos raise `AttributeError` "
"with a suggestion); private attributes (leading underscore) remain free "
"for implementation details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0002-state-and-pure-transfers.md:32
msgid "Alternatives considered"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0002-state-and-pure-transfers.md:34
msgid ""
"**Methods reading `self`**: simpler to write, but the purity would rest "
"on discipline only, and JAX transformations would capture the mutable "
"object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0002-state-and-pure-transfers.md:36
msgid ""
"**Pure functions defined outside the class**: equivalent purity, but "
"scattered code and no natural link between an element and its behaviour."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0002-state-and-pure-transfers.md:39
msgid "Consequences"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0002-state-and-pure-transfers.md:41
msgid ""
"`Values` must become a JAX pytree in phase 2 (P2.5), so that snapshots "
"can be traced and differentiated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0002-state-and-pure-transfers.md:42
msgid ""
"Elements needing pre-computed data (masks, mode profiles) must expose it "
"through fields or through cached helpers computed from `values`, not "
"through hidden attributes read by `transfer`."
msgstr ""
